WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.460
All right, let's get into audience questions
and at least one of them is really funny this

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:09.960
week. Hey David, you famously held Tesla stock
for a long time. Do you regret selling half

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.061
of your Tesla stock since it just went crazy?
Yeah. Earlier this year,

00:00:14.061 --> 00:00:19.240
this week someone had told me that, uh, I
think it was during the Iowa caucus livestream

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:24.430
that day. Tesla's stock closed at seven 80
and as many of you know, I invested in Tesla

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:30.200
when the shares were um, right around $200.
And then I panicked, sold half of it when

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:36.670
Joe Rogan had Elon Musk on and Elon Musk smoked
pot, which I don't care about personally,

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:42.559
but the board went crazy and it looked like
it was trouble for Tesla. I panicked, sold

00:00:42.559 --> 00:00:46.809
half of my stock and I say before, I don't
know what I'm doing with stocks. This is why

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:51.609
I really don't invest in individual stocks.
I only have I think six individual stocks

00:00:51.609 --> 00:00:57.170
and otherwise almost all my money is in a
mutual funds and bonds because I just don't

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:02.249
know what I'm doing. I don't know. I, I do
things like panic sell. So do regret that

00:01:02.249 --> 00:01:08.229
I sold half of the Tesla stock and since then
it must've been at about three 60 when I sold

00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:09.229
half of it.

00:01:09.229 --> 00:01:14.590
And now it's, you know, w it got close to
$800 per share during this week. Yeah. I mean

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:20.040
to some degree I regret it, but at the same
time I know going in individual stocks for

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.659
me are like gambling in that I don't know
when to buy. I don't know when to sell. I'm

00:01:24.659 --> 00:01:29.810
too busy with other things to really be picking
stocks. So the amount of regret is relatively

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:37.899
small. I also, I didn't invest so much that
if I had held all of it right now, my financial

00:01:37.899 --> 00:01:42.159
situation would be drastically different.
And by the way, the things I took it out of

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:47.999
when I sold that half, I put it into other
stocks that have done not as well, but also

00:01:47.999 --> 00:01:52.899
well. So I'm, I don't live in the past to
the extent that I can avoid it. Um, I have

00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:59.539
mild regret, but I think the, the lesson here
is whatever made me buy the Tesla stock to

00:01:59.539 --> 00:02:05.590
begin with years ago when it was at like one
90 or 200 a share that didn't fundamentally

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:11.920
change when Elon Musk smoked pot with Joe
Rogan threatened to take the company private

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:16.510
at four 20 a share to Saudi buyers or something
like that, even though that was a violation,

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:17.510
I guess, of SCC law.

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:21.860
But Hey, you know, I mean, listen, we're,
we're starting to get nitpicky or you know,

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:28.790
whatever else that didn't change the promise
of the company. And now this is one of the

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:33.049
most valuable car companies in history. And
that's really what I should have focused on

00:02:33.049 --> 00:02:38.900
in the same way that my mutual fund strategy
is, you just buy and hold. Because I guess

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:46.170
I believe in the future of the world economy
when I diversify across, you know, total international

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:51.090
stock market index, I'm basically taking a
bet on, I believe in the future of the world

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:58.060
economy. And if, uh, it goes away because
the climate implodes and we have no more planet,

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:03.140
I probably won't care that much about my mutual
funds because we'll all be dead or whatever.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:07.189
In the same way, whatever made me think this
is a good investment for the longterm.

00:03:07.189 --> 00:03:11.830
It didn't have to do with whether or not Elon
Musk was smoking pot with Joe Rogan. So in

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:15.870
retrospect, I should've just gone with the
initial reason I invested in Tesla, which

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:24.280
I thought, uh, I believe that it was a car
company that would become, uh, a, uh, a successful

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:29.310
staple in electric cars. That has happened.
I think 80 or 90% of electric cars on the

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:34.469
road today in the U S are Tesla. Um, and I
should not have panic sold. I regret it, but

00:03:34.469 --> 00:03:36.979
I'm not living with my regret is the way I
would answer the question

